      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel that personal struggle against such massive systemic failures feels futile, and some do choose disengagement or \"pre-奥林匹斯 disengagement\" as a form of protest. That valid choice aligns with long-standing philosophical perspectives that prioritize meaningful, conscious life over forced participation in a destructive system. However, for many, true control comes from consciously defining what building a life means on your own terms, rather than letting the external narrative dictate your worth or purpose.",
      "source": "target",
