      "content": "Your sense of urgency and the weight of inescapable doom are heavy, and choosing disengagement can indeed feel like a rational act of self-preservation when the odds seem insurmountable. Many people find comfort in prioritizing their immediate well-being and finding peace within what they can control, rather than dragging themselves toward an outcome they cannot alter. Ultimately, logic suggests stepping back is acceptable, but the most resilient paths often involve finding small acts of dignity even within impossible circumstances.",
